# Preview checkpoints (rollback)

User may reverse recent preview experiments. Prefer undoing the latest checkpoint first.

## Law (≈ 0.0.444 / harden 0.0.508 / field paint 0.0.510 / cascade 0.0.558) — Preferred + settings cascade

Admin **Preview surface** = **host node + Settings Preferred** (Editable + Display for that one surface).

### Settings cascade (detail → model)

Defaults inherit along the type/composition chain (illustration, not a hard-coded path):

`Präfix → Basiseinheit (BU) → Unit type → Model`

Model / admin Preview / nested cells **must** paint from those presets: Preferred, Q117 Presentation, Hide, Mult, Bindung, walk/Relation overrides. **Good presets ⇒ good final view — only if paint follows settings.**

| Layer | Paint source |
|-------|----------------|
| **Host Preview** | Host Preferred only — Attribute Options / walk Render do **not** switch host Form↔Table chrome |
| **Nested attribute cell** | Attribute type Preferred (`resolveFieldPreferredPaint` / `paintStructureEmbed`) — Compact when Compact is set; **never invent Form** for that layer |
| **Q117 in nested structure** | Type node Presentation (`typePresentation`) — not the outer host |
| **Hide / Mult / Bindung** | Honour walk/edge settings when painting nested schema fields |

### No hardcoding

- **Do not** hard-code by display name, path, or special-case nodes.
- Hardcode **only inside a renderer** for that renderer’s **own** chrome (Form/Table/Compact/Multistep layout mechanics), and **only for the current layer**. Nested content still resolves from the nested type’s Preferred + settings.
- Do **not** paint Form+Table (+Tree) together “for completeness”.
- Do **not** stack CatalogChoice on attribute hosts.
- Empty optional ListChooser / CatalogChoice label is **`—`**, not the word “None”.
- Dispatch: `effectiveHostPreferredRender` → `renderUnifiedPreviewContent` / `renderAttributeHostPreview`.

Plan: [`docs/plans/project-plan.md`](../../docs/plans/project-plan.md) (Presentation surfaces — Settings cascade).
## Checkpoint P4 — Attribute-host Form/Table (≈ v0.0.260–0.0.270)

**Why:** Taxonomy holds **structures**; preview of attribute hosts (Kontakt, Preis, …) needs Form(1 instance) + Table(n instances), each editable + readonly — not the parked Collection `table` type.

**Behavior:** `WTTObjectRender.renderForm` / `renderTable`; field cells via Registry; samples from **name→then type** map (`WTTSampleData`); Kontakt seed under Model; multiplicity swap-vs-clear for required `1`/`1..*`.

**Touch files:** `assets/js/wtt-object-render.js`, `assets/js/wtt-sample-data.js`, `assets/js/tree-admin.js` (`renderAttributeHostPreview`), `includes/class-case-data.php` (`ensure_kontakt_model`), version **0.0.270**.

**Revert P4:** Drop object-render host path; empty rebuild hint for attribute hosts again (keep Sample_Data if other UIs need it).

## Checkpoint P3 — Media MIME + Preferred preview (v0.0.79–0.0.83; Preferred paint ≈ 0.0.523)

**Why:** Q65: one `media` type, different display by MIME. Preview must show what the user selects and how output looks — same law as other Simple leaves: **Preferred (MediaRenderer) → Editable + Display**.

**Kinds:** `image`, `video`, `audio`, `pdf`, `archive` (zip/rar/7z/…), `office`, `text`, `file`, `link`.

**Behavior:** `media` is a Registry type (`MediaRenderer` → `WTTMediaRender.renderField`). Admin Preview uses Preferred Form chrome (Editable = Select/Change/URL; Display = MIME surface). Settings still gate real fields via `allowedKinds` (default none). Sample seed from allowed kinds / sampleEntries.

**Touch files:** `wtt-media-render.js`, `wtt-node-render.js` (`MediaRenderer`), `tree-admin.js` (registry preview + mediaConfig), `class-node-type.php` meta `_wtt_media_allowed_kinds`, version **0.0.523**.

**Revert P3:** Remove MediaRenderer + shared module + allowedKinds meta; restore simple image-or-link surface in admin only.

## Checkpoint P1 — Unit definition vs usage (v0.0.40)

**Why:** Basiseinheit units are schema definitions (Typ=double, Praefix, Kuerzel), not fillable instances. Showing three fake form fields was a style break.

**Behavior after P1:**
- `isBasiseinheitUnit` nodes: **Definition** table (Field / Type / Constraint) + composed **usage** Form/Table (Typ + Praefix + Symbol → e.g. `10.5 mm`)
- Other sets (e.g. Abmessung): unchanged unified Form×{edit,display} + Table×{edit,display}

**Touch files:**
- `assets/js/tree-admin.js` — `isUnitDefinitionNode`, `renderUnitSchemaDefinition`, `renderComposedQuantityControl`, `renderUnitUsageForm` / `Table`, branch in `renderUnifiedPreviewContent`
- `includes/class-tree-admin.php` — i18n: `previewSchema`, `unitSchemaHint`, `unitUsageHint`, `previewColType`, …
- `assets/css/tree-admin.css` — `.wtt-preview-schema*`, `.wtt-preview-quantity*`
- `wp-taxonomy-tree.php` — introduced at **0.0.40** (current plugin ≈ **0.0.74**)

**Revert P1:** Remove the unit-definition branch; again expand unit `setMembers` like any set (Form/Table with all members). Drop schema helpers/CSS/i18n above. Bump or keep patch as needed.

## Checkpoint P2 — Set table = one column (supersedes v0.0.41 member-columns)

**Why:** A **set** is one field. In a table it is **one column**; members (L/B/H, …) render **inside** that cell via `renderSetTableCell` → `renderFieldView`. Spreading members as sibling columns broke the set idea.

**Behavior:** `renderGenericFieldTablePreview(members, setName)` — column header = set/node name; cell = compact member controls. Form layout may still list members as rows.

**Revert to old P2:** call `renderSetMembersTablePreview` again (removed from the hot path).

