## UX rule — Editable preview is interactive

`mode: 'edit'` controls are enabled and write `state.previewValues` (session samples, not term meta). `mode: 'display'` reads the same keys so Display only tracks Editable. Fixed schema values stay read-only.

## UX rule — set = one field

In table context, a set-typed node is **one column**. Members are content of that field, not peer columns. Same for any set (Abmessung L/B/H, unit Typ/Praefix/Kuerzel usage is quantity kind — different kind, still one control).

In **form** context (Editable + Display), a multi-member set is also **one row**: label = `setName (member/names)` via `setFieldCaption` (e.g. `Abmessung (L/B/H)`), controls = same inline cell as the table (`renderSetAsOneFormRow` → `renderSetTableCell` without part labels). **Help** is one `?`: parent `description` first, then members as `helpChildren` underneath (`setFieldHelpPayload` / existing `renderHelpHint`).

## UX rule — set separator + join units

Per set node (editable in **Set settings**):

- **`setSeparator`** (default `/`): used in label `(L/B/H)` and between display values.
- **`setLabelChildren`** (default on; UI: **Include composition in label**): when on, Form + Table labels append composition member names (`Abmessung (L/B/H)`); when off, label is just the set name. Same caption via `setFieldCaption` / `setFieldOptionsFromNode` in Form row, Table column header, and multi-column set columns.
- **`setJoinUnits`** (default on): when all members share the same type **and** that type has a Praefix slot, Display shows magnitudes + separator then the unit once (`10.5/20/5mm`). Editable (quantities): magnitudes with separator + **one shared Praefix** + Kuerzel. Checkbox grayed out when types differ or the type has no Praefix.

## UX rule — short description

Every node may have **`shortDescription`** (term meta): compact expansion of `name` (e.g. L → Länge, m → Milli). Used in set labels, help, and **tooltips** on dropdowns (not inlined in option text).

## UX rule — dropdowns

- Shared builder: `renderOptionsSelect` + `formatSelectLabel` (visible: name/path only).
- `shortDescription` → `<option title>` + closed-select `title` via `syncSelectTitle` (native hover tooltip).
- Branch/Praefix children: `renderBranchSelect` → that builder (node with children).
- No blank `—` placeholder on **required** selects; first real option is selected when nothing matches.
- **Optional** Mult (`0..1` / `0..*` / zero-lower): ListChooser / CatalogChoice **must** offer a clear choice (`None` / `No prefix`) so the field can stay empty (Q116). **No sample fill** for those fields.
- **Required** Mult (`1` / `1..*`): **no** empty/`—` option — pick/swap only. Praefix / Unit prefix selects follow the same Mult law (not “Praefix always empty”).
- Hierarchy indent uses spaces, not dashes (`m` not `— m`).
- Neutral choices use plain labels (`No type`, `Choose node`, `Root (no parent)`).

## UX rule — generic field views (one kind → one view)

Preview controls are **not** hard-coded per domain name (Meter/Abmessung).

1. Normalize input with `asPreviewField(node|member)`.
2. Resolve kind (`quantity` via `quantitySchema` / unit `setMembers`, else scalar type).
3. Render with **`renderFieldView`** only — form rows, table cells, and unit usage samples all call this.

PHP exposes `quantitySchema` for any field whose type is a Basiseinheit **unit** (any unit, not only Meter). Same JSON → same JS view everywhere.

## UX rule — Basiseinheit quantity trinity

Quantity kind = Typ + Praefix + Kuerzel. Example: Abmessung L typed as Meter → same control as Meter’s usage sample.

## UX rule — child extras on parent

For **set** parents (e.g. Meter): show **Child extras** under the parent’s own settings — type / required / fixed / Praefix allowlist+factors. **Not** name/description of children (those stay on the child node). Praefix allowlist+factors is the **same editable view** on the Praefix child and again under the parent (not parent-only).

